#!/bin/sh
# Simple OS – detect live mode and set up the desktop for it
#   simpleos-live --check   exit 0 = live session (started from a USB stick/ISO), otherwise 1
#   simpleos-live --setup   Openbox autostart, at every login:
#     live:       desktop icon "Install Simple OS" (~/Desktop/simpleos-install.desktop), open the Welcome window
#                 once per session (with the install banner); remove Debian's "Install Debian" icon
#     installed:  remove installer icons from the desktop and the installer entry from the Openbox menu
#                 (in case simpleos-post-install could not do that)
# Taskbar badge: simpleos-taskbar-select --apply (asks --check). Menu entry: menu.xml between
# simpleos-installer-begin/-end.
# Detection: kernel parameter boot=live (live-boot) or a mounted live medium (/run/live/medium,
# older live-boot versions /lib/live/mount/medium). The user name alone proves nothing (an installed
# system can also have a user "simple").
# Tests: SIMPLEOS_LIVE=1/0 forces the result, SIMPLEOS_CMDLINE replaces /proc/cmdline.
# No set -e, exit 0 (except --check).

is_live() {
    case "${SIMPLEOS_LIVE:-}" in 1) return 0 ;; 0) return 1 ;; esac
    grep -qw 'boot=live' "${SIMPLEOS_CMDLINE:-/proc/cmdline}" 2>/dev/null && return 0
    [ -d /run/live/medium ] || [ -d /lib/live/mount/medium ]
}

desktop_dir() {
    d=
    command -v xdg-user-dir >/dev/null && d=$(xdg-user-dir DESKTOP 2>/dev/null)
    # without configuration xdg-user-dir returns $HOME itself – then ~/Desktop
    [ -n "$d" ] && [ "$d" != "$HOME" ] || d=$HOME/Desktop
    echo "$d"
}

case "${1:-}" in
    --check) is_live; exit $? ;;
    --setup)
        desk=$(desktop_dir)
        rm -f "$desk/install-debian.desktop"
        if is_live; then
            mkdir -p "$desk"
            if [ -f /usr/share/applications/simpleos-install.desktop ]; then
                cp /usr/share/applications/simpleos-install.desktop "$desk/simpleos-install.desktop"
                chmod 0755 "$desk/simpleos-install.desktop"
            fi
            # Welcome once per session (banner "Install Simple OS Now")
            run=${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-${HOME:-/tmp}/.cache}
            if [ ! -e "$run/simpleos-live-welcome" ] && [ -n "${DISPLAY:-}" ]; then
                touch "$run/simpleos-live-welcome" 2>/dev/null
                (sleep 3; simpleos-welcome) >/dev/null 2>&1 &
            fi
        else
            rm -f "$desk/simpleos-install.desktop"
            menu=${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/openbox/menu.xml
            if [ -f "$menu" ] && grep -q simpleos-installer-begin "$menu"; then
                sed -i '/simpleos-installer-begin/,/simpleos-installer-end/d' "$menu"
                [ -n "${DISPLAY:-}" ] && openbox --reconfigure 2>/dev/null
            fi
        fi
        exit 0 ;;
    *) echo "Usage: simpleos-live --check | --setup" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
